# Generalization And Reusability

- Default to reusable role/module changes over one-off host-specific edits.
- Keep core logic in shared Ansible roles/playbooks; keep per-host values in `host_vars`/`group_vars`.
- Avoid embedding environment-specific names, IPs, usernames, domains, paths, or IDs in reusable templates/tasks.
- Add optional variables with safe defaults instead of hardcoding behavior for a single workload.
- Keep examples generic and copy-paste friendly for future projects.
- For secrets, require vault-backed variables and never commit plaintext tokens/passwords.
- Keep changes idempotent and backward-compatible unless a breaking change is explicitly requested.
- When adding a new capability, document the generic usage path in `docs/` rather than only a single host example.
